&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Knowledge Analyst I with a strong interest in luxury fashion and authentication. In this role, you’ll support Entrupy’s authentication and training workflows by organizing product knowledge, contributing to structured datasets, and building a foundation in authentication best practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role offers hands-on exposure to luxury goods, visual analysis, and knowledge operations, with clear opportunities for growth as you develop expertise and take on increasing responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; Senior Knowledge Analyst&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote - Philippines, India, Hong Kong, Japan, Dubai (UAE)&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location Type: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the maintenance and expansion of Entrupy’s knowledge systems by organizing product information, tagging visual datasets, and updating reference materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in creating and maintaining documentation that supports authentication workflows, including product guides and reference materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct research on luxury brands, collections, materials, and construction techniques to support accurate authentication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor fashion trends, new product releases, and market changes to help keep knowledge assets current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to training and onboarding materials used by the authentication team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quality checks on existing documentation to ensure accuracy, clarity, and consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with senior Knowledge Analysts and cross-functional partners, learning how knowledge supports product and engineering workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gradually take ownership of defined tasks and smaller projects as skills and confidence grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;0–2 years of experience in fashion, luxury retail, authentication, research, merchandising, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in luxury fashion, handbags, and craftsmanship, with a desire to build authentication expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formal authentication experience is a strong plus, but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent attention to detail and a natural curiosity about how products are made and identified.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication skills and the ability to organize information thoughtfully.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with images, structured documents, and basic data tools (such as spreadsheets).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to feedback, a growth mindset, and a strong sense of accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for learning, quality, and upholding standards of authenticity in the fashion industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Culturally, we operate with intelligence, respect, and curiosity, relentlessly pursuing ideas to improve our offering and execute our mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have had an incredible run so far and are laying the foundation for a culture that is fast-paced, entrepreneurial, and rooted in passion, kindness, and positivity. We live by these values – we hire by them, promote them, and celebrate them every day.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are passionate about solving challenging problems in a diverse setup, we’d love to connect!&lt;/p&gt;
